    <item>
      <title>depression subroutines</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/posts/subroutines/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 29 Nov 2022 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/posts/subroutines/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;thinking of how to apply a programming term to the functions inside a human being. That&amp;rsquo;s where this curiosity about the term &amp;ldquo;subroutine&amp;rdquo; started. I haven&amp;rsquo;t yet read extensively about it but as far as I have read, it sounds like something we could say to describe the fundamental &amp;ldquo;wiring&amp;rdquo; of a person too. As was my exploration in Intimate Immensity, this one too wants to deal with what makes us who we are - often without us consciously processing these functions ourselves.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      
